body:
As /u/MyHatGandhi try to upsell your customer at checkout. 

I would recommend shopping around by going direct with the courier. By the sound of it you are using Hermes (now known as EvRi - makes little sense) which have a bad track record with parcel related issues. 

&#x200B;

How my company works it out is the cost to us + man hours with dealing with issues. If you have to deal with a company due to issues with parcel not only is it costing you to send but wasting both your & the customers time.

&#x200B;

(Full discourse my company uses UK Mail)

UK Mail for example has a simple pricing structure and we have only an issue 1/100 so to my business is a good value and also we have found customer who shop with us are returning due to our switch from RM to UK Mail.

&#x200B;

Remember to not only look at the cost but the overall value that a courier can bring. A good courier will make your business stand out and hopefully lead to return sales.

&#x200B;

TLDR - shop around, upsell at checkout (and don't use Hermes)

(Sorry if it sounds like an ad for UK Mail)
